From: Teal Bauer <teal@starsong.eu>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 16:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] apply the Cortex-A9 MP errata workarounds on the DualLite

The DBC builds the Solo board config (MX6S) but the SoC on it is an
i.MX6DL with two Cortex-A9 cores. The multi-core errata workarounds are
gated on !MX6S here, so the board ran with only 743622 applied. They are
secure-mode diagnostic register writes that only the bootloader can do.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific configuration]
---
 include/configs/mx6_common.h | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/mx6_common.h b/include/configs/mx6_common.h
--- a/include/configs/mx6_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/mx6_common.h
@@ -10,8 +10,9 @@
 
 #ifndef CONFIG_MX6UL
 #define CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_743622
-#if (defined(CONFIG_MX6QP) || defined(CONFIG_MX6Q) ||\
-defined(CONFIG_MX6DL)) && !defined(CONFIG_MX6S)
+/* The DBC is an i.MX6DL built with the Solo config: keep the MP errata. */
+#if defined(CONFIG_MX6QP) || defined(CONFIG_MX6Q) ||\
+defined(CONFIG_MX6DL) || defined(CONFIG_MX6S)
 #define CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_751472
 #define CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_794072
 #define CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_761320
